Count the complementary event that the favorite song finishes within the first 4 minutes, 30 seconds. Since it lasts 3 minutes, 30 seconds, it must start at most 60 seconds into the playlist. Two preceding songs would take at least 30 + 60 = 90 seconds. Thus the favorite must be first, or it must be second after the 30-second or 60-second song.
The probability it is first is 1/10. The probability of the second case is (2/10)(1/9): two choices qualify for the first song, and the favorite must be next among the nine remaining songs. These cases are disjoint, so the probability of hearing the entire favorite is 1/10 + 2/90 = 11/90. The requested probability is 1 − 11/90 = 79/90.
Final answer: \dfrac{79}{90}
